7. HOW TO FRAME \'93NETWORKS DECIDE FOR US\'94 WITHOUT OVERCLAIMING\
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\
The phrase is rhetorically powerful, but the paper must define it precisely to\
avoid pushback.\
\
Suggested precise definition:\
\'93Networks decide for us\'94 means that, conditional on fixed individual-level\
propensity distributions and identical innovation attractiveness, the relational\
structure systematically alters adoption outcomes. In this sense, adoption is a\
structural emergent property: the same individuals produce different collective\
behaviors when embedded in different tie configurations.\
\
Avoidable pitfalls:\
- Do not imply individuals have no agency.\
- Do not claim networks are deterministic in all contexts.\
- Do not claim causal identification from observational data alone; your causal\
  leverage is the controlled comparison of network structures within simulation.\
\
Instead, emphasize:\
- counterfactual structure: \'93holding individuals constant, changing structure\
  changes outcomes\'94\
- mechanism: reinforcement pathways and selective influence gates\
